      "content": "Definition: Understandability refers to how easily developers can comprehend and maintain the test code.\n\nTask: Improve the understandability of the test `IndexedCollectionTest_testUnsupportedAdd.java` (path:- /Users/tenghaha/Projects/New_Agent_understandability_improvement/data/original/commons-collections/manual/testcases/IndexedCollectionTest/IndexedCollectionTest_testUnsupportedAdd.java). The refactored code must be syntactically correct and compilable against the provided CUT signatures. Do not alter the runtime behaviour of the original test: the same methods must be called with the same arguments and produce the same expected outcomes.\n"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the structure. The original test has massive boilerplate copied from `AbstractCollectionTest` that's entirely irrelevant to `testUnsupportedAdd`, plus uncompilable code (undefined generic `E`, private abstract methods, missing `IntegerTransformer`). I'll write a clean, focused version that maintains the same runtime behavior (test exits early since `isAddSupported()` returns `true`).The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version strips ~450 lines of unrelated `AbstractCollectionTest` infrastructure (including uncompilable code with undefined generic `E`, private abstract methods, and a missing `IntegerTransformer`), replacing them with a self-contained, focused class that defines `IntegerTransformer` as a static nested class, uses concrete `String` types throughout, and keeps only the methods actually relevant to `testUnsupportedAdd`."
    }
